description:
Before passes 6/7 were scoped to non-activity entities (building_domain-zu4), the live pass-6 run had already written constraints for ~6,553 entities, the majority of them entity_type='activity'. The scoped re-run will NOT touch activities, so these stale activity constraints linger and leave the graph inconsistent with the new policy (no constraints on activities).

TASK: delete constraint rows whose subject entity is an activity, and the matching pass-6 pass_progress rows so the state is clean. Sketch:
  DELETE FROM constraints WHERE subject_id IN (SELECT id FROM entities WHERE entity_type='activity');
  DELETE FROM pass_progress WHERE pass_number='6' AND entity_id IN (SELECT id FROM entities WHERE entity_type='activity');
Verify exact table/column names (constraints subject_id) against the schema before running, and run it AFTER the extraction finishes (not against the live writer). Count rows before/after for an audit trail.
